# AI Codebase Rules - Hexa Match

As an AI assistant working on this codebase, you must follow these rules strictly to conserve token usage, implement high-performance rendering, and maintain codebase health:

## 1. MANDATORY: Read the Source Map & Best Practices First
- Before reading *any* code files in `lib/`, you **MUST** read [source_map.md](file:///Users/dmitrijkabakov/Work/ThirdParty/FlutterApp/VibeGaming/DS3/source_map.md) and [best_practices.md](file:///Users/dmitrijkabakov/Work/ThirdParty/FlutterApp/VibeGaming/DS3/best_practices.md) first.
- Use the map to understand the architecture, and follow the optimization guidelines for rendering, widget rebuilds, and state.
- Do **NOT** open or read entire files unless you are planning to modify them. Rely on these reference guides for structural and logic context.

## 2. Maintain Reference Files
- If you add a new file, change a file path, delete a file, or modify any major API/class relationship, you **MUST** update [source_map.md](file:///Users/dmitrijkabakov/Work/ThirdParty/FlutterApp/VibeGaming/DS3/source_map.md) immediately.
- If you identify new optimization patterns or introduce new core systems, update [best_practices.md](file:///Users/dmitrijkabakov/Work/ThirdParty/FlutterApp/VibeGaming/DS3/best_practices.md).

## 3. High Performance Optimization Mandate
- **Repaint Boundaries**: Wrap animations and static canvas components in `RepaintBoundary` to isolate paint overhead.
- **Widget Rebuild Control**: Decouple state scopes and use `const` widgets where possible to bypass build cycles.
- **Zero Analyzer Warnings**: Static analysis must have zero warnings/errors. Run `flutter analyze` after every code change.

## 4. Git Version Control Protocol
- **Commit & Push**: For each feature or significant task completed, you **MUST** stage, commit, and push the changes to the remote repository.
- **Commit Messages**: Use concise, clear commit messages summarizing what feature was implemented.

## 5. Mandatory Localization Rule
- **All UI Text must be Localized**: Hardcoding raw text strings in UI widgets is strictly forbidden. All labels, buttons, dialogs, tutorial guides, stats, and overlays must be routed through the `AppLocalizations` dictionary system.

